 html←PrepareHtmlPageForDeprecatedList_ major;data;newest;date;version;comment;group
⍝ Returns one row of the list of deprecated packages; see `PrepareHtmlPageForDeprecatedList`.
⍝ `major` is a major version line like "aplteam-APLGit-0". The row leads to its page, says what
⍝ the author said when deprecating it - typically where to go instead - and which release was
⍝ the last one, with a link to its configuration.
 data←1 Reg.ListVersions G.RegistryPath,major
 (newest date)←data[≢data;]                         ⍝ In Tatin's order, so the newest release comes last
 date←(≢'YYYY-MM-DD')↑FormatFloatDate date
 version←newest↓⍨2⊃⍸'-'=newest                     ⍝ All after the name, the hyphen of a beta included
 comment←''GetConfigValue(ReadPackageConfig G.RegistryPath,newest)'deprecateComment'
 group←major↑⍨major⍳'-'                            ⍝ Including the hyphen
 html←'<div class="deprecated-row">'
 html,←'<a class="deprecated-major" href="',Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages/versions/',major,'"><span class="pkg-group-prefix">',(EscapeSpecialChars group),'</span>',(EscapeSpecialChars(≢group)↓major),'</a>'
 :If 0<≢comment
     html,←'<span class="deprecated-comment">',(LinkURLs EscapeSpecialChars comment),'</span>'
 :Else
     html,←'<span class="deprecated-comment none">No reason given</span>'
 :EndIf
 html,←'<span class="deprecated-last">last release <code>',(EscapeSpecialChars version),'</code>, ',date,' · <a href="',Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages/details/',newest,'">config</a></span>'
 html,←'</div>'
⍝Done
